[2026-03-14T20:22:30.788Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JkX3wc1PCW2kgBXSxRdnJB","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me provide you with a comprehensive report of all the findings.\n\n## Google Flights App - Complete Project Overview\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY AND STRUCTURE\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\nGoogleFlights/\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/          # React UI components\n│   ├── pages/              # Page-level components\n│   ├── slices/             # Redux slices\n│   ├── App.tsx             # Main app component\n│   ├── main.tsx            # Entry point\n│   ├── store.ts            # Redux store configuration\n│   └── index.css\n├── netlify/functions/       # Serverless backend functions\n├── tests/                   # Playwright test files (*.spec.ts)\n├── scripts/                 # CLI scripts (seed-db, check, deploy, test)\n├── docs/                    # Documentation\n│   └── tests.md            # Test specifications\n├── playwright.config.ts     # Playwright configuration\n├── vite.config.ts          # Vite build configuration\n├── netlify.toml            # Netlify deployment config\n├── package.json            # Dependencies and scripts\n└── tsconfig.json           # TypeScript configuration\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. DOCS/TESTS.MD - TEST SPECIFICATIONS\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md` (1,413 lines)\n\nThis comprehensive test specification document covers all pages and components with detailed test scenarios:\n\n**Test Categories:**\n\n1. **Search Page (Home)** - Tests for:\n   - TripTypeSelector (6 tests)\n   - PassengerCountSelector (8 tests)\n   - CabinClassSelector (6 tests)\n   - AirportAutocomplete (10 tests)\n   - DatePicker (10 tests)\n   - SearchButton (7 tests)\n   - RecentSearches (5 tests)\n   - PopularDestinations (5 tests)\n\n2. **Search Results Page** - Tests for:\n   - SearchSummaryBar (9 tests)\n   - FilterSidebar (multiple sections)\n   - FlightResultCard\n   - TrackPricesToggle\n   - Pagination\n\n3. **Flight Details & Booking Page**\n4. **My Trips Page**\n\nEach test has:\n- **Components**: List of affected components\n- **Initial state**: Starting conditions\n- **Action**: User interaction\n- **Expected**: Expected outcome\n\n---\n\n### 3. TRIPSTABS COMPONENT SOURCE CODE\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripsTabs.tsx`\n\n```typescript\ninterface TripsTab = 'upcoming' | 'past' | 'tracked'\n\nconst tabs = [\n  { key: 'upcoming', label: 'Upcoming' },\n  { key: 'past', label: 'Past' },\n  { key: 'tracked', label: 'Tracked' }\n]\n\nexport default function TripsTabs()\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Displays 3 tab buttons: Upcoming, Past, Tracked\n- Uses Redux dispatch to set active tab\n- Manages tab state with `setActiveTab` action\n- TestID: `trips-tabs`, `trips-tab-{upcoming|past|tracked}`\n- Styled with BEM CSS classes: `trips-tabs__tab`, `trips-tabs__tab--active`\n\n---\n\n### 4. TRIPCARD COMPONENT SOURCE CODE\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripCard.tsx`\n\n```typescript\ninterface TripCardProps {\n  booking: BookingTrip\n  showCancelButton: boolean\n  onCancel?: (booking: BookingTrip) => void\n}\n```\n\n**Displays:**\n- Airline logo (colored box) with airline code\n- Airline name and flight number\n- Booking status (Confirmed/Cancelled/Completed)\n- Route (origin → destination)\n- Dates (departure, and return if round trip)\n- Total price in USD\n- Booking reference number\n- Cancel button (only for confirmed upcoming bookings)\n\n**Helper Functions:**\n- `formatDate(dateStr)` - Formats to \"MMM DD\"\n- `formatPrice(cents)` - Converts cents to USD format\n- `getStatusClass(status)` - Returns CSS class for status styling\n\n**TestIDs:**\n- `trip-card-{id}`\n- `trip-card-airline-logo-{id}`\n- `trip-card-status-{id}`\n- `trip-card-route-{id}`\n- `trip-card-dates-{id}`\n- `trip-card-price-{id}`\n- `trip-card-ref-{id}`\n- `trip-card-cancel-{id}`\n\n---\n\n### 5. EXISTING TEST FILES (*.SPEC.TS)\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/`\n\n**18 Test Files:**\n1. `airport-autocomplete.spec.ts`\n2. `booking-action.spec.ts`\n3. `cabin-class-selector.spec.ts`\n4. `date-picker.spec.ts`\n5. `filter-sidebar-combined.spec.ts`\n6. `filter-sidebar.spec.ts`\n7. `flight-result-card.spec.ts`\n8. `flight-summary.spec.ts`\n9. `pagination.spec.ts`\n10. `passenger-count-selector.spec.ts`\n11. `passenger-form.spec.ts`\n12. `popular-destinations.spec.ts`\n13. `price-breakdown.spec.ts`\n14. `recent-searches.spec.ts`\n15. `search-button.spec.ts`\n16. `search-summary-bar.spec.ts`\n17. `track-prices-toggle.spec.ts`\n18. `trip-type-selector.spec.ts`\n\n**Example Test (booking-action.spec.ts):**\n- 6 comprehensive tests covering booking workflow\n- Tests: button display, successful booking, reference display, double-booking prevention, loading state, My Trips appearance\n- Uses Playwright's Page object and test helpers\n\n---\n\n### 6. SEED DATA FILE\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` (348 lines)\n\n**Functionality:**\n- Truncates all tables in dependency order\n- Seeds ~50 major international airports (LAX, JFK, LHR, NRT, SYD, etc.)\n- Seeds ~20 airlines (AA, DL, UA, BA, EK, etc.) with logo colors\n- Seeds ~200 flights with realistic routes and prices\n- Creates sample bookings with passengers\n- Creates tracked routes\n- Creates recent searches\n\n**Data Seeding:**\n- Airports: IATA code, name, city, country, lat/long, timezone\n- Airlines: IATA code, name, brand color\n- Flights: Flight number, route, departure/arrival times, duration, aircraft type, amenities (WiFi, power, entertainment), CO2 emissions\n- Prices: All 4 cabin classes with base price, taxes, total, available seats\n- Bookings: Session-based, with booking reference (GF-ABC123 format) and passenger details\n- Flight legs: For multi-segment flights\n\n**Entry Point:**\n```bash\ntsx scripts/seed-db.ts <DATABASE_URL>\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIG\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: './tests',\n  timeout: 60000,\n  expect: { timeout: 10000 },\n  fullyParallel: false,\n  retries: 0,\n  workers: 1,\n  reporter: [['list'], ['json', { outputFile: 'test-results/results.json' }]],\n  use: {\n    baseURL: 'http://localhost:8888',\n    trace: 'on-first-retry',\n    launchOptions: {\n      executablePath: getExecutablePath('chromium'),  // Uses Replay.io\n    },\n  },\n  projects: [\n    {\n      name: 'replay-chromium',\n      use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] },\n    },\n  ],\n  webServer: {\n    command: 'npx netlify dev --port 8888 --functions ./netlify/functions',\n    port: 8888,\n    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,\n    timeout: 30000,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Key Settings:**\n- Test timeout: 60 seconds\n- Expect timeout: 10 seconds\n- Single worker (serial execution)\n- Uses Replay.io for debugging\n- Base URL: http://localhost:8888\n- Auto-starts Netlify dev server\n- Outputs JSON test results to test-results/results.json\n\n---\n\n### 8. NETLIFY FUNCTIONS (TRIPS-RELATED)\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/my-bookings.ts` (100 lines)\n\n**GET `/api/my-bookings?session=<token>`**\n- Fetches all bookings for a session\n- Joins with flights, airlines, airports\n- Returns BookingTrip objects with full flight details\n- Ordered by departure_time ASC\n\n**PATCH `/api/my-bookings`**\n- Updates booking status to 'cancelled'\n- Request body: { bookingId, sessionToken, status: 'cancelled' }\n- Only affects confirmed bookings\n- Returns updated booking with new status\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/tracked-routes.ts` (128 lines)\n\n**GET `/api/tracked-routes?session=<token>`**\n- Returns all tracked routes for session\n- Includes lowest current flight price for each route\n- Joins with origin/destination airports\n- Ordered by creation date DESC\n\n**GET `/api/tracked-routes?session=<token>&origin=<code>&destination=<code>`**\n- Check if specific route is being tracked\n- Returns { tracked: boolean, id: string | null }\n\n**POST `/api/tracked-routes`**\n- Track a new route\n- Request body: { sessionToken, originCode, destCode, departureDateStart?, departureDateEnd?, cabinClass? }\n- Creates or finds session\n- Inserts into tracked_routes table\n\n**DELETE `/api/tracked-routes`**\n- Delete tracked route by ID or origin/destination\n- Request body: { sessionToken, id? | originCode?, destCode? }\n\n---\n\n### 9. TYPES/INTERFACES FOR TRIPS\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/tripsSlice.ts`\n\n```typescript\n// Main booking data structure\nexport interface BookingTrip {\n  id: string\n  booking_reference: string           // e.g., \"GF-ABC123\"\n  cabin_class: string\n  total_price_cents: number\n  status: 'confirmed' | 'cancelled' | 'completed'\n  created_at: string\n  return_flight_id: string | null     // null for one-way\n  flight_number: string\n  departure_time: string              // ISO datetime\n  arrival_time: string\n  duration_minutes: number\n  airline_name: string\n  airline_code: string\n  logo_color: string\n  origin_code: string\n  origin_name: string\n  origin_city: string\n  dest_code: string\n  dest_name: string\n  dest_city: string\n  return_departure_time: string | null\n  return_arrival_time: string | null\n}\n\n// Tracked price monitoring\nexport interface TrackedRoute {\n  id: string\n  departure_date_start: string | null\n  departure_date_end: string | null\n  cabin_class: string\n  created_at: string\n  origin_code: string\n  origin_city: string\n  dest_code: string\n  dest_city: string\n  lowest_price_cents: number | null\n}\n\nexport type TripsTab = 'upcoming' | 'past' | 'tracked'\n\n// Redux state\ninterface TripsState {\n  bookings: BookingTrip[]\n  trackedRoutes: TrackedRoute[]\n  loading: boolean\n  trackedLoading: boolean\n  error: string | null\n  activeTab: TripsTab\n  cancellingBookingId: string | null\n  cancelError: string | null\n  untrackingRouteId: string | null\n}\n```\n\n**Redux Actions:**\n- `fetchMyBookings(sessionToken)` - Async thunk\n- `fetchTrackedRoutes(sessionToken)` - Async thunk\n- `cancelBooking({ bookingId, sessionToken })` - Async thunk\n- `untrackRoute({ routeId, sessionToken })` - Async thunk\n- `setActiveTab(tabKey)` - Sync action\n- `clearCancelError()` - Sync action\n\n---\n\n### 10. ADDITIONAL CONTEXT\n\n**MyTripsPage Component:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/pages/MyTripsPage.tsx`\n- Uses TripsTabs to switch between tabs\n- Renders TripCard for upcoming/past bookings\n- Renders TrackedRouteCard for tracked routes\n- Handles cancel booking with CancelBookingModal\n- Filters bookings by date (now vs past)\n- Session-based using localStorage token\n\n**TrackedRouteCard Component:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TrackedRouteCard.tsx`\n- Displays tracked route with lowest price\n- Shows origin → destination cities\n- Date range or \"Any dates\"\n- Search and Untrack buttons\n- Navigates to results page with tracked route params\n\n**Other Netlify Functions:**\n- `/api/bookings` - Create bookings and fetch flight details\n- `/api/recent-searches` - Save/fetch user's recent searches\n- `/api/flight-legs` - Get flight segment details\n- `/api/search-flights` - Search flights with filters\n- `/api/airports` - Airport autocomplete\n- `/api/popular-destinations` - Featured destinations\n- `/api/explore-dates` - Flexible dates pricing\n- `/api/explore-destinations` - Destination exploration\n- `/api/explore-deals` - Find deals\n\n**Technology Stack:**\n- React 18.3.1 with Vite\n- Redux Toolkit for state management\n- React Router DOM for navigation\n- Netlify Functions for backend\n- PostgreSQL via Neon (serverless)\n- Playwright for end-to-end testing\n- Replay.io integration for test debugging\n\n**Session Management:**\n- Browser localStorage: `gf_session_token`\n- UUID-based session identifiers\n- Session records stored in database for persistence\n\n---\n\nAll files are located in `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/` with the complete source code, test specifications, and configuration available for review."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a270e0fe92ab006b7 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 70082\ntool_uses: 29\nduration_ms: 57585</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05923c41-2ea4-40be-b7d6-bb4c984a6ea5","uuid":"92ab6ffc-1b0a-4a6f-be5b-8092ba21d123","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find the Google Flights app in /repo/apps/. I need:\n1. The app directory name and structure (list key files)\n2. The contents of docs/tests.md (test specifications)\n3. The TripsTabs component source code\n4. The TripCard component source code\n5. Any existing test files (*.spec.ts)\n6. The seed data file\n7. The playwright config\n8. The netlify functions related to trips\n9. Any types/interfaces for trips\n\nBe thorough - read all relevant files completely.","agentId":"a270e0fe92ab006b7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me provide you with a comprehensive report of all the findings.\n\n## Google Flights App - Complete Project Overview\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY AND STRUCTURE\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\nGoogleFlights/\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/          # React UI components\n│   ├── pages/              # Page-level components\n│   ├── slices/             # Redux slices\n│   ├── App.tsx             # Main app component\n│   ├── main.tsx            # Entry point\n│   ├── store.ts            # Redux store configuration\n│   └── index.css\n├── netlify/functions/       # Serverless backend functions\n├── tests/                   # Playwright test files (*.spec.ts)\n├── scripts/                 # CLI scripts (seed-db, check, deploy, test)\n├── docs/                    # Documentation\n│   └── tests.md            # Test specifications\n├── playwright.config.ts     # Playwright configuration\n├── vite.config.ts          # Vite build configuration\n├── netlify.toml            # Netlify deployment config\n├── package.json            # Dependencies and scripts\n└── tsconfig.json           # TypeScript configuration\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. DOCS/TESTS.MD - TEST SPECIFICATIONS\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md` (1,413 lines)\n\nThis comprehensive test specification document covers all pages and components with detailed test scenarios:\n\n**Test Categories:**\n\n1. **Search Page (Home)** - Tests for:\n   - TripTypeSelector (6 tests)\n   - PassengerCountSelector (8 tests)\n   - CabinClassSelector (6 tests)\n   - AirportAutocomplete (10 tests)\n   - DatePicker (10 tests)\n   - SearchButton (7 tests)\n   - RecentSearches (5 tests)\n   - PopularDestinations (5 tests)\n\n2. **Search Results Page** - Tests for:\n   - SearchSummaryBar (9 tests)\n   - FilterSidebar (multiple sections)\n   - FlightResultCard\n   - TrackPricesToggle\n   - Pagination\n\n3. **Flight Details & Booking Page**\n4. **My Trips Page**\n\nEach test has:\n- **Components**: List of affected components\n- **Initial state**: Starting conditions\n- **Action**: User interaction\n- **Expected**: Expected outcome\n\n---\n\n### 3. TRIPSTABS COMPONENT SOURCE CODE\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripsTabs.tsx`\n\n```typescript\ninterface TripsTab = 'upcoming' | 'past' | 'tracked'\n\nconst tabs = [\n  { key: 'upcoming', label: 'Upcoming' },\n  { key: 'past', label: 'Past' },\n  { key: 'tracked', label: 'Tracked' }\n]\n\nexport default function TripsTabs()\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Displays 3 tab buttons: Upcoming, Past, Tracked\n- Uses Redux dispatch to set active tab\n- Manages tab state with `setActiveTab` action\n- TestID: `trips-tabs`, `trips-tab-{upcoming|past|tracked}`\n- Styled with BEM CSS classes: `trips-tabs__tab`, `trips-tabs__tab--active`\n\n---\n\n### 4. TRIPCARD COMPONENT SOURCE CODE\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripCard.tsx`\n\n```typescript\ninterface TripCardProps {\n  booking: BookingTrip\n  showCancelButton: boolean\n  onCancel?: (booking: BookingTrip) => void\n}\n```\n\n**Displays:**\n- Airline logo (colored box) with airline code\n- Airline name and flight number\n- Booking status (Confirmed/Cancelled/Completed)\n- Route (origin → destination)\n- Dates (departure, and return if round trip)\n- Total price in USD\n- Booking reference number\n- Cancel button (only for confirmed upcoming bookings)\n\n**Helper Functions:**\n- `formatDate(dateStr)` - Formats to \"MMM DD\"\n- `formatPrice(cents)` - Converts cents to USD format\n- `getStatusClass(status)` - Returns CSS class for status styling\n\n**TestIDs:**\n- `trip-card-{id}`\n- `trip-card-airline-logo-{id}`\n- `trip-card-status-{id}`\n- `trip-card-route-{id}`\n- `trip-card-dates-{id}`\n- `trip-card-price-{id}`\n- `trip-card-ref-{id}`\n- `trip-card-cancel-{id}`\n\n---\n\n### 5. EXISTING TEST FILES (*.SPEC.TS)\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/`\n\n**18 Test Files:**\n1. `airport-autocomplete.spec.ts`\n2. `booking-action.spec.ts`\n3. `cabin-class-selector.spec.ts`\n4. `date-picker.spec.ts`\n5. `filter-sidebar-combined.spec.ts`\n6. `filter-sidebar.spec.ts`\n7. `flight-result-card.spec.ts`\n8. `flight-summary.spec.ts`\n9. `pagination.spec.ts`\n10. `passenger-count-selector.spec.ts`\n11. `passenger-form.spec.ts`\n12. `popular-destinations.spec.ts`\n13. `price-breakdown.spec.ts`\n14. `recent-searches.spec.ts`\n15. `search-button.spec.ts`\n16. `search-summary-bar.spec.ts`\n17. `track-prices-toggle.spec.ts`\n18. `trip-type-selector.spec.ts`\n\n**Example Test (booking-action.spec.ts):**\n- 6 comprehensive tests covering booking workflow\n- Tests: button display, successful booking, reference display, double-booking prevention, loading state, My Trips appearance\n- Uses Playwright's Page object and test helpers\n\n---\n\n### 6. SEED DATA FILE\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` (348 lines)\n\n**Functionality:**\n- Truncates all tables in dependency order\n- Seeds ~50 major international airports (LAX, JFK, LHR, NRT, SYD, etc.)\n- Seeds ~20 airlines (AA, DL, UA, BA, EK, etc.) with logo colors\n- Seeds ~200 flights with realistic routes and prices\n- Creates sample bookings with passengers\n- Creates tracked routes\n- Creates recent searches\n\n**Data Seeding:**\n- Airports: IATA code, name, city, country, lat/long, timezone\n- Airlines: IATA code, name, brand color\n- Flights: Flight number, route, departure/arrival times, duration, aircraft type, amenities (WiFi, power, entertainment), CO2 emissions\n- Prices: All 4 cabin classes with base price, taxes, total, available seats\n- Bookings: Session-based, with booking reference (GF-ABC123 format) and passenger details\n- Flight legs: For multi-segment flights\n\n**Entry Point:**\n```bash\ntsx scripts/seed-db.ts <DATABASE_URL>\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIG\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: './tests',\n  timeout: 60000,\n  expect: { timeout: 10000 },\n  fullyParallel: false,\n  retries: 0,\n  workers: 1,\n  reporter: [['list'], ['json', { outputFile: 'test-results/results.json' }]],\n  use: {\n    baseURL: 'http://localhost:8888',\n    trace: 'on-first-retry',\n    launchOptions: {\n      executablePath: getExecutablePath('chromium'),  // Uses Replay.io\n    },\n  },\n  projects: [\n    {\n      name: 'replay-chromium',\n      use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] },\n    },\n  ],\n  webServer: {\n    command: 'npx netlify dev --port 8888 --functions ./netlify/functions',\n    port: 8888,\n    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,\n    timeout: 30000,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Key Settings:**\n- Test timeout: 60 seconds\n- Expect timeout: 10 seconds\n- Single worker (serial execution)\n- Uses Replay.io for debugging\n- Base URL: http://localhost:8888\n- Auto-starts Netlify dev server\n- Outputs JSON test results to test-results/results.json\n\n---\n\n### 8. NETLIFY FUNCTIONS (TRIPS-RELATED)\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/my-bookings.ts` (100 lines)\n\n**GET `/api/my-bookings?session=<token>`**\n- Fetches all bookings for a session\n- Joins with flights, airlines, airports\n- Returns BookingTrip objects with full flight details\n- Ordered by departure_time ASC\n\n**PATCH `/api/my-bookings`**\n- Updates booking status to 'cancelled'\n- Request body: { bookingId, sessionToken, status: 'cancelled' }\n- Only affects confirmed bookings\n- Returns updated booking with new status\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/tracked-routes.ts` (128 lines)\n\n**GET `/api/tracked-routes?session=<token>`**\n- Returns all tracked routes for session\n- Includes lowest current flight price for each route\n- Joins with origin/destination airports\n- Ordered by creation date DESC\n\n**GET `/api/tracked-routes?session=<token>&origin=<code>&destination=<code>`**\n- Check if specific route is being tracked\n- Returns { tracked: boolean, id: string | null }\n\n**POST `/api/tracked-routes`**\n- Track a new route\n- Request body: { sessionToken, originCode, destCode, departureDateStart?, departureDateEnd?, cabinClass? }\n- Creates or finds session\n- Inserts into tracked_routes table\n\n**DELETE `/api/tracked-routes`**\n- Delete tracked route by ID or origin/destination\n- Request body: { sessionToken, id? | originCode?, destCode? }\n\n---\n\n### 9. TYPES/INTERFACES FOR TRIPS\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/tripsSlice.ts`\n\n```typescript\n// Main booking data structure\nexport interface BookingTrip {\n  id: string\n  booking_reference: string           // e.g., \"GF-ABC123\"\n  cabin_class: string\n  total_price_cents: number\n  status: 'confirmed' | 'cancelled' | 'completed'\n  created_at: string\n  return_flight_id: string | null     // null for one-way\n  flight_number: string\n  departure_time: string              // ISO datetime\n  arrival_time: string\n  duration_minutes: number\n  airline_name: string\n  airline_code: string\n  logo_color: string\n  origin_code: string\n  origin_name: string\n  origin_city: string\n  dest_code: string\n  dest_name: string\n  dest_city: string\n  return_departure_time: string | null\n  return_arrival_time: string | null\n}\n\n// Tracked price monitoring\nexport interface TrackedRoute {\n  id: string\n  departure_date_start: string | null\n  departure_date_end: string | null\n  cabin_class: string\n  created_at: string\n  origin_code: string\n  origin_city: string\n  dest_code: string\n  dest_city: string\n  lowest_price_cents: number | null\n}\n\nexport type TripsTab = 'upcoming' | 'past' | 'tracked'\n\n// Redux state\ninterface TripsState {\n  bookings: BookingTrip[]\n  trackedRoutes: TrackedRoute[]\n  loading: boolean\n  trackedLoading: boolean\n  error: string | null\n  activeTab: TripsTab\n  cancellingBookingId: string | null\n  cancelError: string | null\n  untrackingRouteId: string | null\n}\n```\n\n**Redux Actions:**\n- `fetchMyBookings(sessionToken)` - Async thunk\n- `fetchTrackedRoutes(sessionToken)` - Async thunk\n- `cancelBooking({ bookingId, sessionToken })` - Async thunk\n- `untrackRoute({ routeId, sessionToken })` - Async thunk\n- `setActiveTab(tabKey)` - Sync action\n- `clearCancelError()` - Sync action\n\n---\n\n### 10. ADDITIONAL CONTEXT\n\n**MyTripsPage Component:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/pages/MyTripsPage.tsx`\n- Uses TripsTabs to switch between tabs\n- Renders TripCard for upcoming/past bookings\n- Renders TrackedRouteCard for tracked routes\n- Handles cancel booking with CancelBookingModal\n- Filters bookings by date (now vs past)\n- Session-based using localStorage token\n\n**TrackedRouteCard Component:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TrackedRouteCard.tsx`\n- Displays tracked route with lowest price\n- Shows origin → destination cities\n- Date range or \"Any dates\"\n- Search and Untrack buttons\n- Navigates to results page with tracked route params\n\n**Other Netlify Functions:**\n- `/api/bookings` - Create bookings and fetch flight details\n- `/api/recent-searches` - Save/fetch user's recent searches\n- `/api/flight-legs` - Get flight segment details\n- `/api/search-flights` - Search flights with filters\n- `/api/airports` - Airport autocomplete\n- `/api/popular-destinations` - Featured destinations\n- `/api/explore-dates` - Flexible dates pricing\n- `/api/explore-destinations` - Destination exploration\n- `/api/explore-deals` - Find deals\n\n**Technology Stack:**\n- React 18.3.1 with Vite\n- Redux Toolkit for state management\n- React Router DOM for navigation\n- Netlify Functions for backend\n- PostgreSQL via Neon (serverless)\n- Playwright for end-to-end testing\n- Replay.io integration for test debugging\n\n**Session Management:**\n- Browser localStorage: `gf_session_token`\n- UUID-based session identifiers\n- Session records stored in database for persistence\n\n---\n\nAll files are located in `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/` with the complete source code, test specifications, and configuration available for review."}],"totalDurationMs":57585,"totalTokens":70082,"totalToolUseCount":29,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1329,"cache_read_input_tokens":65176,"output_tokens":3576,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1329},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
